{
  "_doc": "Unlocks (docs/gdd/03b_diversion_y_ritmo.md §3b.4, O-D2 a): each mechanic arrives when the player needs it, with its card «Nuevo: …», a mark on the HUD button that opens it, its tutorial chapter and a goal in the goals zone. Unlocks.step (sim/pacing/unlocks.gd) watches the triggers of each human family and writes state.unlocks[fam][id] = {minute, seen, used}; what an unlock opens is UI access (ui: the buttons that stay hidden until then: staff, upgrades), never a rule of the sim. trigger: start (the game's first step) · calendar {day: from that day index (0 = day 1 of spring, year 1)} · gold {min: family gold} · title {min: title id, by rank} · employees {min: employees of the family} · age {min: the head's age} · event {event, match, count: events of the family, as the objectives} · outsold_rival (a day with more units sold at the market than the rival smith's family) · any [triggers] (the first one that holds) · all [triggers]. window: [first, last] day index where 3b.4 expects it (the pacing bot checks it ±1 day). mark: the HUD or interior button that gets the «Nuevo» mark until used (\"\" none). chapter: the tutorial chapter offered on the card (data/tutorial/). goal: an objective of data/objectives/ shown as an open goal of `horizon` (short, medium, long) once unlocked (§3b.5.1). card: false = no card (the start's own mechanics, shown by the tutorial). requires: a system not in the game yet: the unlock waits until data/<requires>.json or data/<requires>/ exists (its hook).",
  "goals_doc": "§3b.5.1: the open goals zone shows up to 3 goals: short = the current start objective (or the first open one of the day), medium = the goal of the latest unlock not done, long = the year's (the debt in year 1) or the dynasty's (data/goals.json). Each one {horizon, objective, from}.",
